{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQExtDerivUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQExtDerivUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq_determined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq_determined","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv-unique.lean#L93-L111","doc":"**The derived q-derivative is determined by the data (proved).**\nGiven the same Frobenius–Hopf object and the same `(d, π_V, q)`,\nthe derived morphism `d_q = q⁻¹ d + (1 − q⁻¹) π_V ≫ d` agrees. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.unique","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv-unique.lean#L52-L91","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical q-exterior derivative (proved\nextensionality).**\n\nTwo `CategoricalQExtDeriv C` instances with the same Frobenius–Hopf\nobject and the same data `(d, π_V, q)` are equal.\n\nNote there is deliberately **no hypothesis about `qinv`**, even\nthough it is a data field. It is determined: `q * qinv = 1` and an\ninverse in a commutative monoid is unique. The structure acquired\n`qinv` when `q_ne_zero` was replaced by `q * qinv = 1` — `R_q =\nℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is a ring with no `Inv` instance, so the inverse must be\ncarried as data — and this file's `rfl` was left behind by that\nmigration. Adding a `qinv` hypothesis would have made the file\ncompile while weakening the theorem; deriving it keeps the\nstatement as strong as the narrative claims.\n\nHistorically this also replaced a **false** `axiom : Subsingleton\n(CategoricalQExtDeriv C)`: the structure bundles its object and\ncarries free data, so distinct instances plainly exist. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-q-ext-deriv-unique","label":"prop:categorical-q-ext-deriv-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}